// Short-range self-centered cone of fire -- circle 1, deliberately small
// radius (must NOT scale to high circles per the sheet's own note).
// `Shockwave`'s only shipped precedent as a player spell is circle 3-4
// (pulse_wave/crimson_lash, both ~90-116 energy / ~50-56 damage / 8-9m
// travel via shockwave_speed*duration) -- no circle-1 sibling exists yet, so
// energy/damage/travel here are scaled down proportionally from that pair
// rather than copied outright; a self-calibrated judgment call, not a
// structural balance decision.
// `knockback` is Shockwave's own inherent mechanic (every shipped Shockwave
// spell has one) even though D&D's Burning Hands has no forced-movement
// rider -- kept minimal (strength 3) rather than removed, since the variant
// has no "no knockback" mode. Documented simplification, not a sheet-fidelity
// miss.
Shockwave(
    energy_cost: 45,
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    swing_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    damage: 24.0,
    poise_damage: 6,
    knockback: (strength: 3.0, direction: Away),
    shockwave_angle: 90.0,
    shockwave_vertical_angle: 45.0,
    shockwave_speed: 12.0,
    shockwave_duration: 0.4,
    dodgeable: Jump,
    move_efficiency: 0.1,
    damage_kind: Fire,
    specifier: Fire,
    ori_rate: 1.0,
    timing: PostBuildup,
    emit_outcome: true,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(9.0)),
)
